<title>UK: Union says London postal strike cancelled for now.</title>
<headline>Union says London postal strike cancelled for now.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Postal services strikes in central London, planned for today and next Monday, have been withdrawn as Communication Workers Union (CWU) on Friday temporarily lifted its industrial action threat.</p>
<p>The decision to suspend the strikes was taken after recent talks enjoyed some progress, the CWU said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;Some progress was made at the (June 24) meeting and it was decided to withdraw Friday's and Monday's action to give negotiators an opportunity to find a solution to the problems,&quot; said Norman Candy, London Divisional Representative for the CWU.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4364</p>
</text>
